BEHAVIORAL CHANGES (compatible, no code changes needed):
- AtomicFIFO informer behavior (enabled by default): store state updated atomically before handler callbacks. Multus uses SharedIndexInformer for pods and netdefs - compatible.
- UnlockWhileProcessing (enabled by default): informers can enqueue during processing. No impact on multus informer patterns.
- Resync processing improvements: timing differences in handler invocations. No tight timing dependencies in multus.
- WatchListClient feature: may affect SharedInformer usage but can be disabled via feature gate.

DEPRECATIONS (still functional, future cleanup recommended):
- fake.NewSimpleClientset() deprecated in favor of fake.NewClientset() - used in 3 test files (k8sclient_test.go, thick_cni_test.go, multus_suite_test.go). Still compiles.
- record.EventRecorder deprecated in favor of events.EventRecorder - used in cert-approver/main.go and k8sclient.go. Still compiles.
- metav1.FieldsV1.Raw direct access deprecated - not used by multus.
- Service .spec.externalIPs deprecated - not used by multus.
- httpstream/spdy/wsstream deprecated - not used by multus.

GO VERSION: go.mod requires go 1.26.0, k8s 1.36 built with Go 1.26.2-1.26.4. Compatible.

KUBELET PODRESOURCES API: DRA extensions (KubeletPodResourcesDynamicResources) graduated to GA. Multus uses podresources/v1 API (PodResourcesListerClient, DynamicResource, ClaimResource, CDIDevice) - all stable, no breaking changes.

CERTIFICATES API: Multus cert-approver uses certificates/v1 (CertificateSigningRequest) - stable, no breaking changes. New PodCertificateRequest fields (stubPKCS10Request) not relevant.

CLIENT-GO DISCOVERY: Discovery() still returns DiscoveryInterface in v0.36.2 (DiscoveryInterfaces change not yet in tagged release). Multus only calls .Discovery().ServerVersion() - compatible.

PROTO: ProtoMessage() removal from API types - multus does not use protobuf serialization directly. Uses kubelet gRPC (separate proto), unaffected.

CONCLUSION: All k8s.io dependencies already bumped to v0.36.2. No compile-breaking changes affect multus-cni. Behavioral changes in informers are compatible with multus usage patterns. Deprecations are non-blocking.

